.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt HOSTAPD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm hostapd ,
.Nm hostapd_cli
.Nd Wi-Fi access point
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm hostapd
.Op Fl hdBKtvqS
.Op Fl P Ar pidfile
.Op Fl e Ar entropy
.Op Fl f Ar logfile
.Op Fl g Ar global_ctrl
.Op Fl G Ar group
.Op Fl i Ar ifname Ns Op , Ns Ar ifname ...
.Ar config ...
.Nm hostapd_cli
.Op Fl i Ar ifname
.Op Fl p Ar dir
.Op Ar command
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm hostapd
is hostap's access point, version 2.12.
It runs the interfaces that each
.Ar config
describes as access points through the kernel's nl80211 interface, and
authenticates the stations that join them.
.Pp
Rach2 builds it statically with OpenSSL, beside
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8 ,
with SAE for WPA3-Personal, 802.11n, and an integrated EAP server with
PEAP, TTLS and TLS, and MSCHAPv2, GTC and MD5 inside them, so that it
offers open networks, WPA, WPA2, WPA3, WPA3's transition mode and
WPA2-Enterprise.
No Rach2 image stages it: it is the access point of the Linux guest of the
Wi-Fi suite.
.Pp
.Nm hostapd_cli
sends a command to a running hostapd through the control interface that
.Cm ctrl_interface
names in its configuration, or reads commands from the terminal when none
is given.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl B
Run in the background.
.It Fl d
Print more of what happens; given twice, more still.
.It Fl e Ar entropy
Keep random state across runs in the file
.Ar entropy .
.It Fl f Ar logfile
Append the messages to
.Ar logfile
instead of the standard output.
.It Fl g Ar global_ctrl
Open a global control interface at
.Ar global_ctrl .
.It Fl G Ar group
The group that owns the control interfaces.
.It Fl h
Print the usage and exit.
.It Fl i Ar ifname
Use these interfaces instead of the
.Cm interface
of the configurations.
.It Fl K
Print keys in the messages.
.It Fl P Ar pidfile
Write the process number to
.Ar pidfile .
.It Fl q
Print less; given twice, less still.
.It Fl S
Start all the interfaces together.
.It Fl t
Begin some messages with the time.
.It Fl v
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
A WPA2 and WPA3 network in transition mode on channel 6:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
interface=wlan0
driver=nl80211
ctrl_interface=/var/run/hostapd
ssid=home
hw_mode=g
channel=6
wpa=2
wpa_key_mgmt=WPA-PSK SAE
rsn_pairwise=CCMP
ieee80211w=1
wpa_passphrase=a long passphrase
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr iw 8 ,
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
